Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Preserve mouse capture on keyboard type changes.

Switching between devices with different macOS keyboard types generates
KEYBOARD_CHANGED even when the input source and Windows keyboard layout
remain the same. Sending WM_CANCELMODE for this type-only change releases
mouse capture in legacy WoW while its mouse buttons are still held.

Keep rebuilding the key tables and activating the layout, but only send
WM_CANCELMODE when NtUserActivateKeyboardLayout returns a different HKL.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/keyboard.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/keyboard.c
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/keyboard.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/keyboard.c
@@ -1044,7 +1044,9 @@ void macdrv_keyboard_changed(const macdrv_event *event)

     macdrv_compute_keyboard_layout(thread_data);

-    NtUserActivateKeyboardLayout(thread_data->active_keyboard_layout, 0);
-
-    send_message(get_active_window(), WM_CANCELMODE, 0, 0);
+    /* A different physical keyboard can require new key tables without changing
+     * the input source. Do not cancel mouse capture for such type-only changes. */
+    if (NtUserActivateKeyboardLayout(thread_data->active_keyboard_layout, 0) !=
+        thread_data->active_keyboard_layout)
+        send_message(get_active_window(), WM_CANCELMODE, 0, 0);
 }
